{"graph_chars": "Good morning. I am Professor Elsa Voss. This lecture covers Chapters One and Two of Principles of Macroeconomics, OpenStax, third edition. Chapter One is Welcome to Economics. Chapter Two is Choice in a World of Scarcity. We start with scarcity, division of labor, micro versus macro, the circular flow, economic systems, FRED, and globalization. Then we take the next step: opportunity cost, the budget constraint, utility, the production possibilities frontier, comparative advantage, and Adam Smith's invisible hand. The opening case of Chapter One is about decisions under imperfect information in an age of social media. Economists treat information as incomplete, yet people still make hundreds of decisions each day. Markets are affected by how well and how fast information moves. To post or not to post is an economic decision, because every choice uses scarce time. Chapter Two adds the punch line the Rolling Stones already knew: you cannot always get what you want.", "graph_times": [[0.0, 0.0636], [0.0636, 0.1272], [0.1272, 0.1908], [0.1908, 0.2544], [0.2544, 0.318], [0.318, 0.3816], [0.3816, 0.4452], [0.4452, 0.5088], [0.5088, 0.5724], [0.5724, 0.636], [0.636, 0.6996], [0.6996, 0.7632], [0.7632, 0.8268], [0.8268, 0.8904], [0.8904, 0.954], [0.954, 1.0176], [1.0176, 1.0812], [1.0812, 1.1449], [1.1449, 1.2085], [1.2085, 1.2721], [1.2721, 1.3357], [1.3357, 1.3993], [1.3993, 1.4629], [1.4629, 1.5265], [1.5265, 1.5901], [1.5901, 1.6537], [1.6537, 1.7173], [1.7173, 1.7809], [1.7809, 1.8445], [1.8445, 1.9081], [1.9081, 1.9717], [1.9717, 2.0353], [2.0353, 2.0989], [2.0989, 2.1625], [2.1625, 2.2261], [2.2261, 2.2897], [2.2897, 2.3533], [2.3533, 2.4169], [2.4169, 2.4805], [2.4805, 2.5441], [2.5441, 2.6077], [2.6077, 2.6713], [2.6713, 2.7349], [2.7349, 2.7985], [2.7985, 2.8621], [2.8621, 2.9257], [2.9257, 2.9893], [2.9893, 3.0529], [3.0529, 3.1165], [3.1165, 3.1801], [3.1801, 3.2437], [3.2437, 3.3073], [3.3073, 3.371], [3.371, 3.4346], [3.4346, 3.4982], [3.4982,